  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1... \nWe will see an increase in moisture Sunday especially with mid \nand high clouds from a Nor'easter. Areas closest to the \nAppalachian ridge will see light rain chances Sunday afternoon\nand evening, especially up in the Clarion and Jefferson County\nPA areas. Eastern Ohio will remain far enough west to remain\ndry. With the increased cloud cover, daytimes highs drop back \ninto the upper 60s on Sunday.\n\nPrecipitation is possible Wednesday night into Friday when the \nridge breaks down allowing a shortwave trough passage. While\nthis system is likely to pick up tropical moisture from the\nremnants of Pacific Hurricane Polo, much of the heavier rain\nthreat is likely to stay west of our forecast area. \n\nAs of now, the probability of measurable precipitation remains \nbetween 30%-40% Wednesday night and Thursday and increases to \n30-50% Friday. Probability of 24 hour QPF >=0.10\" Wednesday \nnight is 10-20%, increasing to 20-30% Thursday and 40-50% \nFriday.",
